            <h3>Tips to Save Money on This Route </h3>
            <p>Managing the cost of train travel from Portland to Seattle is easier with some planning and smart strategies. Prices can vary depending on timing, class, and travel season, but with the right approach, you can save money without compromising comfort. </p>
            <p> Plan for Better Price Options</p>
            <ul>
                <li> <b> Advance Booking: </b>  Purchasing tickets days or weeks ahead often secures the lowest fares, especially for Coach seating. Cascades fares can start as low as $27 with early purchase.</li>
                <li> <b> Compare Departures: </b>  Check multiple departure times to find the most economical option - midday trains are often cheaper than peak morning or evening services.</li>
                <li> <b> Seating Choices: </b>  Coach is generally cheaper than Business Class; consider if comfort trade-offs are acceptable for shorter 3.5-hour journeys.</li>
                <li> <b> Amtrak Guest Rewards: </b>  Sign up for Amtrak's loyalty program to earn points toward future travel.</li>
            </ul> <h3>Arrival at the Station in Portland </h3>
            <h3>Travel During Off-Peak Hours </h3>

            <ul>
                <li> <b>Midday Trains: </b>  Often less crowded, with fares sometimes lower than early morning or evening trains.</li>
                <li> <b>Avoid Peak Travel: </b>  Friday evenings, Sunday afternoons, holidays, and popular times often lead to higher prices and limited availability.</li>
                <li> <b>Flexibility Helps: </b> Traveling on Tuesdays or Wednesdays can reduce cost and provide a more relaxed environment with better seat selection.</li>
