            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

            <h3>1. How long is the train from Portland to Seattle? </h3>

            <p>The train journey typically takes 3 hours 25 minutes to 4 hours, depending on the service (Cascades vs Coast Starlight) and the number of stops. </p>

            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from Portland to Seattle? </h3>

            <p>The fastest option is Amtrak Cascades, which can complete the journey in approximately 3 hours and 25 minutes with direct service. </p>

            <h3>3. How much does a train ticket from Portland to Seattle cost? </h3>

            <p>
                Ticket prices generally fall between:
                $27-$45 for early booking
                $45-$75 for standard fares
                $75-$110+ for last-minute or Business Class travel
            </p>

            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from Portland to Seattle? </h3>

            <p>Yes, all Amtrak Cascades and Coast Starlight trains on this segment are direct, so there's no need for transfers. </p>

            <h3>5. What amenities are available onboard? </h3>

            <p>Trains offer comfortable seating (no middle seats), Wi-Fi (where available), power outlets at every seat, a bistro car with local craft beverages, and luggage space. </p>

            <h3>6. Is train travel faster than driving? </h3>

            <p>Depending on traffic, driving may take 2.5-4 hours on I-5, while the train is generally stress-free, predictable, and scenic - especially during rush hour or bad weather. </p>

            <h3>7. Can you travel from Portland to Seattle in one day? </h3>

            <p>Yes, the route is well-suited for same-day trips, with 4-7 daily departures. Early morning trains get you to Seattle by mid-morning, and evening trains return you to Portland by late night. </p>

            <h3>8. Which station in Portland do trains depart from? </h3>

            <p>Most trains depart from Portland Union Station, located in downtown Portland. Some airport connections are available via MAX Light Rail from PDX, but require extra planning. </p>

            <h3>9. Which station do trains arrive at in Seattle? </h3>

            <p>Trains arrive at Seattle King Street Station, conveniently located in the city center (Pioneer Square) and easily accessible by Link Light Rail, buses, and rideshare. </p>

            <h3>10. Is Business Class worth it? </h3>

            <p>Yes, Business Class offers extra legroom, a quieter environment in a dedicated bistro car section, priority boarding, and complimentary non-alcoholic beverages - making it ideal for travelers seeking more comfort during the 3.5-4 hour journey. </p>





